WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.338
- Welcome back to the show.
I'm not David S Pumpkins.

00:00:03.338 --> 00:00:05.838
(funky music)

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:07.763
(whip crack)

00:00:07.763 --> 00:00:10.160
Today's program will remind
all you kids out there

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.980
be careful what you wish for.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.550
You want a loyal best buddy
or a pot of gold at the end of

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.610
the rainbow, be my guest.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.800
Or rather, be their victim.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.170
In one corner, we have Chucky,
the tortuous toy trickster

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:23.350
and his opponent,

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.660
the limericking,
limestone-laden Leprechaun.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.527
- You may feel some pain.

00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:31.220
'Tis a pity I forgot me Novocaine

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.160
- These two have transcended the confines

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.600
of the horror movie genre

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.490
and have permanently cemented themselves

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:39.560
in both the pop culture
lexicon and our nightmares.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.990
Heck, you can even catch them

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:44.160
on every football Saturday and Sunday!

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.100
Sports are the ultimate escape

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.490
but there is no running from
these tiny Tinseltown terrors.

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:51.375
Here's how we'll determine a winner:

00:00:51.375 --> 00:00:53.307
Round one: Box office.

00:00:53.307 --> 00:00:56.930
Round two: Tomatometer/audience score.

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:59.156
Round three: Creation story.

00:00:59.156 --> 00:01:01.340
And then I'll do a wild card round

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:02.410
that's going to prove this is

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.020
the ultimate duel of diminutive devils.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:07.370
On the line, a fresh pot of gold against

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.590
a Toys 'R' Us shopping spree.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:11.040
Even though I'm fairly certain

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.220
Geoffrey the giraffe's doors are closed.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.410
And that gold, let's face it,

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:17.650
it's probably just foil encasing
for subpar milk chocolate.

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:18.760
Hey, I ain't complaining.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.750
Chucky's got his game face ready,

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:23.140
the Leprechaun wore his
best river dancing boots,

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.300
So let's get it on.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.133
- It's

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:26.520
showtime.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:29.557
- You won't beat me,
'cause I'm a leprechaun.

00:01:30.955 --> 00:01:32.712
- (bell rings) Round one: Box office.

00:01:32.712 --> 00:01:36.070
In past episodes of Vs,
when we talk box office,

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.660
it's usually boffo.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.760
Billions of dollars are
tossed around with regularity

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:42.360
and while I don't get to keep any of it,

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.700
it's no secret why some other franchises

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.310
have remained so popular.

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.384
Money talks, but for Child's
Play and Leprechaun movies?

00:01:49.384 --> 00:01:51.590
Uh, yeah, let's not start looking

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:53.744
at winter homes in Florida just yet.

00:01:53.744 --> 00:01:54.740
- Shit!

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:57.630
- To date, only the first two
of the eight Leprechaun films

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.000
have been given a proper
theatrical release.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.100
Remember when he danced
an Irish jig on the moon

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.690
or sang about the multiple
definitions of booty

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.450
in Leprechaun in the Hood?

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.450
Yeah, we enjoyed those on home video.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:12.270
The franchise has just grossed
$24 million in domestic coin,

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.070
making for an average of
12 million per outing.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:17.213
But even if we give the little leper,

00:02:17.213 --> 00:02:18.920
that didn't sound healthy,

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.660
a wide release for all eight films?

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.636
Chances are he still can't
play with the Chuckster.

00:02:23.636 --> 00:02:25.470
- I want respect!

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:26.980
- Child's Play came out in the eighties,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.880
the decade before sentient toys became

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.530
our cuddliest Pixar
pals and sliced its way

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:34.630
to an impressive $78
million domestic haul.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.700
Sequels and more profit would follow

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.170
until The Curse of Chucky

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.650
and then The Cult of Chucky
decided to head directly

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.020
to Video Update.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:45.040
That was the Williamsburg,
Virginia version of Blockbuster.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:46.450
I still owe them late fees.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:49.510
- I can't think of a thing to say.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:51.890
- All told, six of the
eight Child's Play flicks

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:54.090
sold tickets at movie
theaters and they combined

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:57.580
for a $286 million franchise tag.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:01.386
That makes for a $47.6
million per flick average.

00:03:01.386 --> 00:03:04.990
Somehow, that still surpasses
the gross of the recent reboot

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:07.420
featuring Mark Hamill
as the voice of Chucky,

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:10.000
which finished its run at $29 million.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.210
Leprechaun can compete with that number,

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.830
but given the Chuckster's head
start in the horror heyday

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:17.647
of the 1980s and his consistent
presence in theaters,

00:03:17.647 --> 00:03:20.470
(bell rings) it's an
easy round one victory.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.534
So easy, you might say
it's... child's play?

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:24.388
- What.

00:03:24.388 --> 00:03:25.280
- You're right.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.520
I deserve to have a green
goblin curse me forevermore

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.280
for making that dad joke.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.617
- Don't fuck with the Chuck!

00:03:31.617 --> 00:03:34.900
- (bell rings) Round two:
Tomatometer/audience score.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.870
Okay, Leprechaun, it's your lucky day

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.240
because now that we're
done with the finances,

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.980
let's talk about your pot of gold.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:43.450
- Have I mentioned that I want me gold?

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.580
- Specifically, how did critics feel

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:48.850
about your extreme methods
in protecting said treasure?

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:50.009
Oh, it's not good.

00:03:50.009 --> 00:03:51.630
Here's the bright spot.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:53.740
The underappreciated
Leprechaun in the Hood

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:55.300
is at 30%!

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:56.600
And Leprechaun Returns,

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.630
the most recent entry in the franchise,

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:02.063
has the highest percentage
of all his movies at 44!

00:04:02.063 --> 00:04:03.520
We're trending upward,

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:07.007
which is my sugarcoated way
of saying here's the bad news.

00:04:07.007 --> 00:04:11.037
Three of the Leprechaun flicks are at 0%.

00:04:11.037 --> 00:04:12.560
- Zero

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.570
point

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:14.880
zero.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.840
- The one that started
it all and introduced us

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:20.980
to Jennifer Aniston
pre-Rachel cut is just at 23%.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:25.005
So, this all makes for an
average film score of 16.6%.

00:04:25.005 --> 00:04:26.900
But, hey, these are horror movies,

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:29.680
they never sit well with
the critics, said the person

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:31.990
who doesn't have a
teleprompter in front of them.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:36.060
I know because Child's Play
movies do pretty darn well.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:39.410
Half of the films in the
franchise, get this, are fresh.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:41.970
That's four movies about a murderous doll

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:44.463
that critics said, yep, that's cinema.

00:04:46.694 --> 00:04:47.527
- What are you looking at?

00:04:47.527 --> 00:04:49.710
- 71% is the score for the original flick

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:50.940
that started it all.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:52.880
Then Curse of Chucky broke the curse

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.887
of direct to Red Box and earned a 76%.

00:04:55.887 --> 00:05:00.358
Cult of Chucky then set
the all-time high at 79%.

00:05:00.358 --> 00:05:03.600
The most recent reboot
is also fresh at 63%,

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:06.197
so it's been a nice turnaround for Chuck.

00:05:06.197 --> 00:05:09.650
His lowest movie is Child's Play 3 at 29%,

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:12.860
but overall he's still on
the outskirts of Fresh Town

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:15.689
with a 55% average for eight movies.

00:05:15.689 --> 00:05:18.680
This doll can kill you with
a knife or the kind words

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:21.840
movie reviewers have
given him over the years.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.120
- You fucking with me?

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.720
- Okay, okay, but that audience score

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.640
has got to favor the Leprechaun, right?

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:28.770
I mean, he was referenced
in Wayne's World.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:31.179
- Garth, I'm the Leprechaun!

00:05:31.179 --> 00:05:32.336
- Cool it, okay.

00:05:32.336 --> 00:05:34.920
- Unfortunately, it appears
most of the audience?

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.270
Sided with Garth.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.260
Leprechaun does better in this frame

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:40.980
but his 30% average is still dwarfed,

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:42.208
oh, sorry about that,

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:43.737
(spooky flute music)

00:05:43.737 --> 00:05:45.665
by Chucky's 53% average.

00:05:45.665 --> 00:05:47.490
Curse of Chucky is the doll's peak

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:50.560
on the audience side of things at 76%

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:53.070
and the closest the
Irish troll gets to fresh

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:56.526
is a respectable 48%
for Leprechaun Returns.

00:05:56.526 --> 00:05:59.370
Which, if you're keeping
score at home, is 2% higher

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.170
than Constantine, staring Keanu Reeves!

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:05.210
Sorry, Jacqueline Coley,
maybe Rotten Tomatoes is

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.270
wrong?

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:08.317
Enjoy our podcast wherever
you listen to stuff.

00:06:08.317 --> 00:06:09.640
- Fine!

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:10.711
All right, already.

00:06:10.711 --> 00:06:13.040
- (bell rings) Child's Play
takes round two and it appears

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:15.930
the Leprechaun has just
about reached the end

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.520
of his rainbow.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.250
- I am Chucky,

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:20.738
the killer doll!

00:06:20.738 --> 00:06:22.104
And I dig it!

00:06:22.104 --> 00:06:22.937
(thunder clap)

00:06:22.937 --> 00:06:25.900
- (bell rings) Round
three: Creation story.

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.670
The Fighting Irish football team has been

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:30.620
mythologically great
at late game comebacks.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:33.480
And if Leprechaun wants to
prove he's the next Joe Montana,

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:36.000
it'll take one convincing tall tale.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.497
Ah, I said tall.

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:38.730
My bad.

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:39.670
- About three-foot-six.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:40.920
- [woman] Three-foot-six?

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:45.040
- Yeah, but I make up
for it in other areas.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:47.660
- Creator Mark Davis wanted
to make a horror movie.

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:48.681
You know what inspired him?

00:06:48.681 --> 00:06:50.020
Yep.

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:51.260
Lucky Charms.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.720
He saw an ad for the cereal,

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:54.510
which I ate not two hours ago,

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.740
and the rest is cinematic history.

00:06:56.740 --> 00:06:58.490
- Fuck you, Lucky Charms.

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:01.050
- So, while the actual genesis
of the movie franchise itself

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:05.180
is giggle-worthy, the war of
the Leprechaun is dead serious.

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:08.330
Each movie spins a slightly
different version of the tale.

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:11.710
Our villain can be anywhere
from 600 to 2000 years old.

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:14.241
Originally, he got his pot of gold stolen,

00:07:14.241 --> 00:07:16.780
chased it across the
Atlantic to North Dakota,

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:18.920
where he got boxed there
for 10 years before escaping

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:19.753
in go-karts.

00:07:19.753 --> 00:07:20.586
(engine rattle)

00:07:20.586 --> 00:07:22.520
- Ring around the rosie!

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:25.180
- Since then, his mission
has varied from revenge,

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:27.930
like in Back to the
Hood, to finding a bride,

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:29.123
as seen in part two.

00:07:29.123 --> 00:07:32.170
He went to Los Angeles to
achieve the bride goal.

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:34.883
Good luck, pal, the line
starts right behind me.

00:07:35.833 --> 00:07:38.985
- Something new, something old,

00:07:38.985 --> 00:07:41.080
let's be together

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.360
on Leprechaun's gold.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:46.940
- Based on the war in Origins,
he may actually be a God!

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:49.550
Or at least a being with
supernatural powers,

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:52.370
ones that keep him in statue
form until a medallion

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:55.740
is removed from the adorable
lawn ornament exterior.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:57.450
It's tough to keep up
with all that creativity

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.840
but Chucky doesn't care.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:01.010
His story has remained
comparatively steadfast

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:02.800
but no less compelling.

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:05.560
The Lakeshore Strangler
managed to transfer his soul

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:09.210
into a Good Guy doll by way
of voodoo just before he died.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:10.470
The Strangler's name?

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:11.780
Charles Lee Ray.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:12.613
Why?

00:08:12.613 --> 00:08:14.040
Because of course it is.

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:17.060
Never trust someone who
goes by three names,

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:18.400
they could be a killer.

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:20.730
- I'm not ashamed to be a killer.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:22.380
I'm proud of it.

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:25.221
It's not an addiction, it is a choice

00:08:25.221 --> 00:08:27.660
and it is not something that you should

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:29.790
have to hide in the closet.

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:30.830
- Even the good ones!

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:33.760
Keegan-Michael Key murders us
all with his delightful comedy

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:37.720
and David Lee Roth slaughters
rock arenas around the globe.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:39.580
I don't even trust F. Scott Fitzgerald.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:42.150
He killed Jay Gatsby, right?

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:44.010
As for the old sport, Chucky, the magic

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:45.490
isn't just in his creation,

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:47.790
it's in his multiple resurrections.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.100
Yeah, he's been brought back to life

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:51.730
by electrical malfunctions, stitching,

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.580
some of his blood falling into a vat

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:55.670
used to make more Good Guy dolls.

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:57.570
That's a bad day at the plant.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:58.900
And in the most recent version,

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:01.780
AI was the cause of him
coming back to life.

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:04.980
Don Mancini is the genius
behind Child's Play.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.500
He wrote seven of the scripts
and directed three films

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:08.610
in the franchise.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:11.170
And while the origin story
of his beloved evil creation

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:12.660
gets points for consistency,

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:15.560
the greatness of Leprechaun
lies in the fact that

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:18.100
none of us really know how we
got here in the first place.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:22.210
And thus, how the hell do we
game plan in case he returns?

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:25.270
Both evil entities have proven
they'll never really die

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:26.440
but if we're going off of who had

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:27.890
the most interesting birth?

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:29.810
I have to apologize to
everyone in New Orleans,

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:32.190
particularly that one woman
that worked in the store in the

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:34.060
French Quarter that I'm
pretty sure cursed me

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:35.540
after a comedy show.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:38.000
Voodoo is powerful and I respect it.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.600
But what are all the kids trying to take?

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:40.991
Me Lucky Charms!

00:09:40.991 --> 00:09:42.760
- (bell rings) Leprechaun wins round three

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:44.550
and is back in the game.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.825
- Oh, so you know the Lep

00:09:46.825 --> 00:09:48.831
is the real OG.

00:09:48.831 --> 00:09:50.060
- (bell rings) And now it's time for

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:52.980
the Wild card round: Iconic moments.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:56.090
This is where the luck of
the Irish could come up huge.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:57.990
Even for a monster that needs an EpiPen

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.910
if he's around four leaf clovers.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:01.980
Say what you want about
lackluster box office

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.240
or Rotten Tomato meters,

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:06.090
both Chucky and the Leprechaun
are firmly entrenched

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:08.210
in the cultural zeitgeist for a reason.

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:11.410
They've given us plenty of
highlights over the years.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:12.760
- Hello, Andy.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:14.190
- Going back to the first Child's Play,

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:16.600
Chuck has always had a
flare for the dramatic.

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:19.180
He used a voodoo doll to killed Dr. Death

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:20.970
and as impressive as a start as that is,

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:23.470
what I consider to be
the most iconic would be

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.420
how he met his bride-to-be.

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:28.180
It's the classic story
we were all told as kids.

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:31.750
Grandpa dumped a TV into
the bathroom to off Grandma.

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:34.620
The movie playing on said
television at the time?

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:35.840
Bride of Frankenstein.

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:37.970
It works on so many levels.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:41.130
- Hey, Raggedy Anne, you
looked in the mirror lately?

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:43.250
Now's not the time to get picky.

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:45.530
- Chucky has wreaked havoc
on folks with his go-to

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:47.160
weapon of choice, a butcher knife.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.440
- So, were you born with that knife

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:50.620
super glued onto your hand or what?

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:53.630
- But occasionally, he goes to
the bench and calls in, say,

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.520
an ax in Curse of Chucky,

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:57.760
a yard stick in Child's Play 2

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:59.030
or how about Child's Play 3,

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:00.840
when he throws the proverbial kitchen sink

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.160
at this poor fella.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.040
Is that a golf club and

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:05.400
a yo-yo?

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:07.760
Major points for creativity, buddy.

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:12.160
- Nothing like a strangulation
to get the circulation going.

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:14.240
- His counterpart is
also a gifted improviser,

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.926
as the leprechaun has utilized
everything from a pogo stick

00:11:16.926 --> 00:11:20.980
to a lawnmower blade to make
memorable deaths in his movies.

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:24.225
A personal favorite is when
Leprechaun, in outer space,

00:11:24.225 --> 00:11:27.560
sneaks his essence into
a guy's body via pee,

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:29.670
then transfers himself into another person

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:32.780
when those two morons
decided to do the nasty.

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:34.229
- Holy shit!

00:11:34.229 --> 00:11:35.290
(Chucky laughs)

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:37.010
And they call me sick?

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:38.530
- Sadly, this is not the first time

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:40.520
I've had to remind folks
watching this show,

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:43.230
do not have sex in space.

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:44.670
Why is this so difficult?

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:46.760
It should be like day one of NASA school.

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:48.490
Thank you, class, see you tomorrow

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:52.120
when we'll talk about how
to not pee on a tiny corpse.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:54.450
It's a dead body, not snow.

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:56.463
- Let that be a lesson to you, lad.

00:11:56.463 --> 00:11:58.580
- Besides that flick being my favorite one

00:11:58.580 --> 00:11:59.800
to bring up at dinner parties,

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:02.650
it also features a light saber kill.

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:05.300
Fitting, because who plays the Leprechaun?

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:08.640
Yep, Star Wars veteran Warwick Davis.

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:09.970
He borrowed that laser sword

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:13.140
from the latest voice of
Chucky and never gave it back.

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:16.040
But my favorite gruesome kill
in any of the Leprechaun films

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:19.071
has got to be in the 0% fresh part three,

00:12:19.071 --> 00:12:22.611
when a poor woman combusts
in front of our eyes.

00:12:22.611 --> 00:12:27.440
Or in part two, when a guy gets
a pot of gold in his tummy.

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:28.700
Or in Back in the Hood,

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:30.880
when some poor sat meets
his demise at the hands of

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:32.651
a bong-wielding Leprechaun.

00:12:32.651 --> 00:12:35.921
Look out, Californians, that
could happen to any one of us.

00:12:35.921 --> 00:12:39.570
(Leprechaun coughs and laughs)

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:42.320
- Each fella has a wicked
smart sense of humor.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:44.390
Chucky loves a good
laugh and the Leprechaun

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:47.670
kicked off his franchise
featuring a wheelchair chase scene

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:50.640
that rivals the Rascal
scooter chase from Seinfeld.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:52.140
Both these are horror movies,

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:55.750
so what's the truly most
terrifying scene from each set?

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:57.331
For Chucky, it's when we all find out

00:12:57.331 --> 00:12:59.310
he ain't running on batteries.

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:00.490
It's in the very first film

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:02.940
and when that knowledge meets
the fact that he survived

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:04.130
a gunshot?

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:05.360
Look out.

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:07.990
- Sometimes I scare myself.

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:09.930
- This rampaging Ruxpin is going to be

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:11.570
running with the devil long after

00:13:11.570 --> 00:13:13.510
the Energizer Bunny peters out.

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:15.180
For good old greeny, I'm going to go

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:16.730
with more recent offerings.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.850
It's a toss-up between Leprechaun Returns,

00:13:18.850 --> 00:13:20.920
when he pops out a poor Ozzy's stomach,

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:23.363
or in Origins, when he shows
the world, he may be old

00:13:23.363 --> 00:13:26.134
but he still plays video games.

00:13:26.134 --> 00:13:27.440
Fatality.

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:29.680
Chucky is great and has
given us a closet full

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:30.900
of memories to cherish

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:33.230
but the lengths the
Leprechaun has gone for us

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:34.960
cannot be denied.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:37.460
The trip from Ireland is
worthy of consideration

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:40.868
but then to go to the hood
twice and outer space?

00:13:40.868 --> 00:13:44.740
Again, the Leprechaun went to outer space.

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:46.130
And flattened a guy.

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:47.411
It's so gnarly.

00:13:47.411 --> 00:13:49.830
(bell rings) Leprechaun gets
the win in the wildcard round

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:51.820
and we got us a tied ball game.

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:54.193
- I'm the man of green come to do no good,

00:13:54.193 --> 00:13:56.338
Lep in the hood come to do no good.

00:13:56.338 --> 00:13:58.600
Lep in the hood come to do no good.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:01.080
- Yes, it's been a back
and forth slug fest

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:02.455
that has resulted in a tie.

00:14:02.455 --> 00:14:04.746
But did you tune in to see a draw?

00:14:04.746 --> 00:14:06.440
What, do you think Chucky and Leprechaun

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:07.860
are just gonna shake hands, buddy up

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:10.950
and go live with Annabel
in the next great sitcom?

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:13.532
Devil Babies is filmed before
a live studio audience.

00:14:13.532 --> 00:14:16.115
(upbeat music)

00:14:21.089 --> 00:14:23.257
♪ It's a rare condition ♪

00:14:23.257 --> 00:14:24.840
- Uh, Ubu ain't gonna sit for that

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.530
and I know you folks want a winner.

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:28.810
So, here we go with one final question:

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:30.690
Who'd win in a fight?

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:32.250
Leprechaun is much older,

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:35.020
but that could prove wiser
against his younger opponent.

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:38.020
Chucky does have just as many
movies under his overalls

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:40.230
and although he doesn't have
the frequent flyer miles

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:42.450
of his elder, he does have voodoo.

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:44.610
That could counteract Leprechaun's magic.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.670
And if Chucky gets his hands on the gold,

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:49.140
it might further reduce
Leprechaun's powers.

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:51.238
Both fellas tend to have
a weakness for the ladies

00:14:51.238 --> 00:14:54.290
but it's my estimation that
Leprechaun has more holes

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:55.348
in his game than Chuck.

00:14:55.348 --> 00:14:58.710
Four leaf clover, iron,
eating Count Chocula

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.010
instead of Lucky Charms.

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:02.738
Chucky has assets that work
against the Leprechaun.

00:15:02.738 --> 00:15:04.120
And he's got a whole cult

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:07.130
and a loving bride that
could jump into the fracas.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:09.720
Binging the Leprechaun
movies is an Ellis family

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:11.480
St. Patrick's Day tradition.

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:13.330
But if he ever runs across Chucky,

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:14.750
all the grain in the world

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:16.437
won't save him from getting pinched.

00:15:16.437 --> 00:15:19.100
(bell rings) No shame in
losing to a doll, Leprechaun,

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:21.280
especially one voiced by Brad Dourif.

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:22.530
- You know?

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:23.810
I love being me.

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:25.890
- And I love my job.

00:15:25.890 --> 00:15:27.900
- I'm fucking infamous.

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:30.660
- Chucky wins but that's
just according to my book.

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:32.120
And I can barely read.

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:34.380
Now it's your turn, my lovely viewers.

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:36.680
Comment below, vote with your pick.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:38.930
Is it the box office king Chucky

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:41.750
or the magical mystery of the Leprechaun?

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:44.360
I can't wait to have somebody
else read me your take

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.560
and I'll leave you with
what your senior quote

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:47.423
should have been.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:49.910
I'll take it from you, homie, you'll see,

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:52.353
'cause you know the
Leprechaun is the real OG.

00:15:53.214 --> 00:15:55.797
(upbeat music)

